    "lhs": "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left( (x^2 + 1)^2 \\right) =",
    "mistakes": [
     {
      "expr": "2(x^2 + 1)",
      "why": "The power rule is for $x^n$, not for $(x^2 + 1)^n$. Expand: $(x^2 + 1)^2 = x^4 + 2x^2 + 1$, then differentiate term by term."
     },
     {
      "expr": "4x^3 + 2x",
      "why": "$\\frac{d}{dx}\\left( 2x^2 \\right) = 4x$: the factor 2 stays."
     },
     {
      "expr": "4x^3 + 1",
      "why": "The constant 1 has derivative 0, and $2x^2$ has derivative $4x$."
     }
    ]
   },
   "why": {
    "correct": "$(x^2 + 1)^2 = x^4 + 2x^2 + 1$, so the derivative is $4x^3 + 4x$."
   }
